    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "CONTINUOUS FROM SCENE 9"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "No blackout."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The Roman Announcer has gone. The marketplace immediately breaks into urgent motion."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The people who were gossiping moments ago suddenly have their own problems: routes, family lines, supplies, money, children, travel."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The Roman motif continues briefly beneath the chaos."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph is no longer listening to the complaints. He is calculating."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary sees his face."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Joseph?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "We have to go to Bethlehem."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Bethlehem?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "My family line. The House of David."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Beat."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "That’s where I have to register."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "How far?"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph hesitates."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Joseph."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Far."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "How far is “far”?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Far enough that I don’t want you making the journey."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "No."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Mary—"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "No."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Listen. You can stay here. I’ll register and come back as quickly as I can."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "We just decided we weren’t doing the difficult things apart."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "This is different."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Why?"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Beat."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Because this difficulty has a road?"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph knows exactly what she means."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I’m trying to protect you."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary steps closer."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Then protect me while we walk."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "That stops him."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary offers her hand."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Together."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph takes it."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Together."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "PREPARATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "music",
      "text": "MUSIC SHIFTS INTO PREPARATION / JOURNEY UNDERSCORE"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The village moves quickly around them. No long farewell sequence. Every friend arrives with a purpose."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Shira gives Mary a blanket."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SHIRA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Take this."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "You need it."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SHIRA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I have another."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary looks at her."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "No, you don’t."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SHIRA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Then I’ll get another."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "A small smile."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SHIRA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Come back."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "They embrace briefly."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Adina arrives with practical supplies."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "ADINA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Food. Water. Extra cloth."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Caleb appears carrying far too much."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CALEB"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "And I brought everything else."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Ezra inspects the pile and removes one item."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "EZRA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "No."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CALEB"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "What?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "EZRA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "They’re going to Bethlehem, not opening a restaurant."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CALEB"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Joseph?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Listen to Ezra."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CALEB"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Marriage has changed you."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph keeps packing."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Levi approaches with a staff."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "LEVI"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Take it."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Levi gives Joseph a traveling staff"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Levi does not leave."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "LEVI"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I still don’t understand half of what you’re doing."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I know."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "LEVI"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Doesn’t mean I’m sending you out unprepared."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph looks at him."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I know that too."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "They clasp forearms. No larger reconciliation is needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Malachi approaches."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MALACHI"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Take care of them."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph looks toward Mary."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Malachi reads the old fixer instinct in him."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MALACHI"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "And let her take care of you."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph looks back at him."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I’ll try."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MALACHI"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Good."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Nia and Simon slip through the adults."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Nia holds a small handmade item."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "NIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "For the baby."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Nia..."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "NIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "It’s small. He’ll be small."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SIMON"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "At first."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Everyone looks at Simon."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SIMON"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Babies grow."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "NIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "We know, Simon."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary laughs."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "She accepts the gift."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The preparations are finished before anyone is ready for them to be."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "DEPARTURE"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The village opens a path."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary and Joseph look back at Nazareth."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Do not sentimentalize the farewell. This is still the town that has just judged them, and still the home that contains the people they love."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Shira stays close to the edge. Caleb lifts a hand. Levi stands farther back. Nia and Simon watch."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "A faint “Walk With You” motif emerges."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph reaches for Mary’s hand."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary takes it."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "They begin."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Nazareth does not vanish at once. It recedes."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Then the road takes over."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "THE JOURNEY"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The ensemble creates distance rather than literal geography."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Bodies, fabric, travelers, light, wind, and changing horizons form the road."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The LED moves from the recognizable Nazareth horizon into wider, less protected country. Slow environmental motion only."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Light shifts through morning, afternoon, and evening."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Moderate haze may make distance and moving shafts of light visible, but it must read as atmosphere—not magic."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The movement vocabulary repeats: PACK → LIFT → WALK → STOP → BREATHE → WALK AGAIN."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "EARLY JOURNEY"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Still all right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "They walk."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "And now?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Still yes."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "More road."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph looks at her again."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Joseph."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I didn’t say anything."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "You were thinking it."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I was."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Think quieter."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph smiles."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "They continue."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph studies the road ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "We should reach the next stopping place before dark."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "You planned that?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I was afraid you’d stopped planning."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I’ve grown spiritually."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Beat."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I haven’t lost my mind."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary laughs."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The humor is affectionate. Planning itself is not Joseph’s flaw; believing a plan can guarantee the future is."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The music carries them forward."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "TIME PASSES"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "No dialogue for a stretch."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Day becomes night."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary rests."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph covers her."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "He checks the road, then catches himself checking it again."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Instead of waking Mary or rearranging everything, he sits."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Dawn."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "They walk again."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "More travelers pass in both directions."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The terrain grows harder."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The movement phrase repeats with more ground time between actions."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary begins to slow."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "FATIGUE"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph notices immediately."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "How are you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I need a minute."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph helps her to a safe place to rest without taking over her movement."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "He gives her water."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Then he looks down the long road."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "We should’ve stopped sooner."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Joseph—"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I should’ve found another way. More help. Something—"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Joseph."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "He stops."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "You don’t have to fix every hard thing."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Beat."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Just stay with me."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph looks at her."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Then, instead of scanning the road for another solution, he lowers himself beside her."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I’m here."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary takes his hand."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "That’s enough."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Allow real stillness here. The road continues around them for a few seconds while they do not move."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph cannot make the road shorter, Caesar disappear, Bethlehem closer, or Mary less tired."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "For once, presence is the action."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "ONE MORE STEP"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary takes a breath and prepares to stand."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph offers support without pulling her up."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "One more step."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "One more step."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "They rise together."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "A tiny musical fragment may surface—not a new number, simply memory."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY & JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Walk with me..."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "They continue."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The journey phrase resumes: WALK → STOP → BREATHE → WALK AGAIN."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "THE WARNING"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Time compresses."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Another stretch of road. Wind. Travelers. Changing light."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Then Mary stops."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Her breath catches."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph turns instantly."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Mary?"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary raises one hand: wait."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph waits."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "He does not pepper her with questions."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The moment passes."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Was that—"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I’m all right."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Beat."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "She is listening to her own body."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "But we should keep moving."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph understands."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The underscore gains urgency without becoming melodramatic."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "They move."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "BETHLEHEM"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The horizon changes."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph sees it first."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Mary."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "She looks."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Bethlehem."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Relief."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "transition",
      "text": "Finally."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "They share a tired smile."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Then the city reveals itself."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Crowds. Travelers. Bundles. Families. Animals. Noise. Arguments. Doors."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The visual arc completes: COMMUNITY → COUPLE → VASTNESS → CROWD."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Nazareth knew them too well. Bethlehem does not know them at all."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary takes in the scale of it."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "Oh."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "It’s..."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Crowded."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Very."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary looks at him."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "We only need one room."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph takes that as a solvable problem."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Exactly."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Beat."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "One room."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "He spots a lodging place."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "They cross."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "KNOCK. KNOCK."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "A door opens."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Excuse me. My wife needs a place to rest."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "INNKEEPER"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "No room."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "DOOR SHUTS."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Silence."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph looks at the closed door."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Then at Mary."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary looks at him."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "For the briefest instant, the old Joseph wants to solve the whole city at once."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Instead, he takes a breath."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "All right."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "He looks toward the next door."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Next one."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "He moves."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "KNOCK. KNOCK."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "No blackout."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The next knock belongs to Scene 11."
    },
    {
      "type": "transition",
      "text": "END SCENE 10"
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "NOTES"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Scene 10 should feel like the musical suddenly accelerates. After several emotionally heavy scenes, the conflict becomes physical: distance, fatigue, preparation, crowds, and time. The source specifically calls for a lean scene with no full song—Rome gives us the initial disruption, then the journey is carried primarily through movement, underscoring, and short dialogue."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "I’m also carrying forward both Nia and Simon in the departure, but keeping them brief so they do not slow the journey."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The strongest relationship payoff in this scene is"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "MARY: “You don't have to fix every hard thing. Just stay with me.”"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "JOSEPH: “I'm here.”"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "That continues Joseph's builder arc without repeating it. The source specifically identifies this section as the point where Joseph discovers that he cannot make the road shorter, Mary's body less tired, Caesar disappear, or Bethlehem come closer; Mary's lesson is that presence can sometimes be enough when fixing is impossible."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "I would also protect the progression of the journey visually: community → couple → vastness → crowd. They leave Nazareth surrounded by people who know them perhaps too well, spend the road increasingly alone together, then arrive in Bethlehem surrounded by strangers who do not know them at all. That contrast prepares “No Room” before a single innkeeper rejects them."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "And ending Scene 10 literally on “No room” with no blackout gives Scene 11 immediate momentum—the first rejection is not the climax; it is only the beginning."
    }
  ]
}
